nd overcast, with drizzle and mist in places, all day. Runners had 11 hours to complete the course.\n\nPiet VORSTER claimed the men's title in 05:45:02, ahead of Johnny HALBERSTADT (05:50:30) and Bruce FORDYCE (05:51:15). Jan MALLEN won the women's race in 08:22:41, followed by Moira HORNBY (08:29:10).\n\nPiet VORSTER's 05:45:02 set a new up record, beating Alan ROBB's 05:47:00 from 1977. Jan MALLEN set a new women's course record of 08:22:41, surpassing Lettie VAN ZYL's 08:25:00 from 1978. Jan MALLEN's 08:22:41 was faster than the men's winning time as recently as 1922 (Arthur NEWTON, 08:40:00).\n\nFrom a field of 2,823 entries, 2,820 runners completed the course for a 99.9% finish rate. The field comprised 2,809 men and 11 women (0.4% female). The average finish time was 09:00:41.\n\nMedals awarded: 10 Gold, 344 Silver, 2,466 Bronze. 1,105 runners (39.2%) were completing their first Comrades. The final finisher was DEAN in 10:59:19.\n\nCompared to the previous up run in 1977, the field was 69.1% larger.","countryDataPct":0.0}